  "dry_snp_activity": "On the Capesize sector, Chinese buyers acquired the “AASHNA” - 180K/2012 HHIC for region USD 37 mills. On the same sector, the scrubber fitted “NICHOLAS G.S” - 179K/2010 Sungdong was sold for low/mid USD 34 mills to Chinese buyers. Moving down the sizes, on the Post Panamax sector, the “INDUS PROSPERITY” - 93K/2011 Taizhou Sanfu changed hands for USD 11.5 mills to Chinese buyers basis DD due and poor condi- tion. On the Ultramax sector, “BRITA OLDENDORFF” & “BENJAMIN OLDENDORFF” both 62K/2020 Oshima were sold enbloc for USD 37.5 mills each, Meghna ac- quired the “CMB JORDAENS” - 63K/2019 Tadotsu for USD 35.2 mills, while the “INCE BEYLERBEYI” - 61K/2012 Iwagi was sold to ADNOC for region USD 22 mills. On the Supramax sector, the Electronic M/E “IVS CRIMSON CREEK” - 58K/2014 Shin Kurushima found new owners for mid USD 23 mills Finally, on the Handysize sector, the OHBS “IKAN LANDUK” 37K/2013 Onomichi was sold for very high USD 16 mills and the “BLUE UNION ALPHA” - 28K/2011 Imabari was sold for USD 9.65 mills.",
  "wet_snp_activity": "This week’s tanker S&P activity saw a fair number of transactions. In the Suezmax sector, the sister vessels “ALASKA” - 163K/2006 HHI and “ARCHANGEL” - 163K/2006 HHI were sold enbloc to Chinese buyers for USD 50.75 mills each. Moving down to the MR seg- ment, the 1A ice classed “MINERVA RITA” - 50K/2005 STX changed hands for USD 16.2 mills to Chinese inter- ests. In the smaller sizes, the Stainless Steel unit “FG ROTTERDAM” - 19K/2012 Usuki was reported sold for high USD 22 mills. The Scrubber fitted and StSt “DING HENG 39” - 19K/2008 Fukuoka, achieved USD 18.3 mills basis. Finally, the Stainless Steel “CNC DREAM” - 19K/2004 Fukuoka was concluded at USD 11.5 mills.",
